DING GTK 4: stabilize Wayland desktop window placement and inhibit suspend.

Upstream DING v105 (MR !527) switched from map to window-created with a single
250ms move_frame timer, dropped position/minimize/fullscreen/stacking guards,
never recomputed target (x, y) on workarea or monitor updates, and left the
GTK4 Wayland surface vulnerable to Mutter's XDG_TOPLEVEL_STATE_SUSPENDED after
3s of window occlusion (causing desktop icons to vanish permanently after
minimizing or closing a covering window, upstream #379).

Recompute target coordinates dynamically, enforce desktop type and placement
across first-frame/map/position-changed/size-changed/unlock, guard stacking
without dual-monitor loops, and attach a 1x1 zero-opacity Clutter.Clone to keep
Mutter's MetaWindowActor suspend state inhibited.

Upstream component: https://gitlab.com/rastersoft/desktop-icons-ng

